From: Martin <gsp4045@cyberperseus.com>
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] j7200: restore UDMA for HyperFlash image reads

The minimal SD configuration uses SDHCI ADMA and disables NAVSS UDMA.
Restore UDMA and its channel API for the existing CFI dma_memcpy path.
Select this fragment after the minimal and HyperFlash fragments on A72;
keep SPL DMA disabled and leave R5 unchanged.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [J7200 HyperFlash boot configuration]

diff --git a/configs/j7200-a72-hyperflash-dma.config b/configs/j7200-a72-hyperflash-dma.config
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/configs/j7200-a72-hyperflash-dma.config
@@ -0,0 +1,4 @@
+# Restore the CFI mem-to-mem DMA path in U-Boot proper only.
+CONFIG_TI_K3_NAVSS_UDMA=y
+CONFIG_DMA_CHANNELS=y
+# CONFIG_SPL_DMA is not set
